        }
      //std::cout &lt;&lt; "curly brace constructor\n";
    }

c counts the elements of L read so far; only the first NT are copied into v (if (c &lt; NT)), the others are ignored: a longer list never writes outside the array.
The second for has no initialization: it starts from the current c and sets to 0 the components the list did not give: pvector C = {4.0}; is (4,0,0).

